            <ArticleTitle>Office pediatric otology.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>781-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Office pediatric otology requires the management of some of the most common acute and chronic conditions of childhood. Some of these conditions include eustachian tube dysfunction, otorrhea, granulation polyps, extruded tubes, otitis media, trauma, otalgia, and sudden hearing loss. An approach that recognizes the concerns of the child and parent facilitates the examination and treatment with minimal discomfort.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
